<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/4th-century-bce">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · War</p><h1 class="enc-title">Corinthian War</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">395–387 BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/4th-century-bce">4th century BCE</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Corinthian War was fought from 395 to 387 BCE between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sparta">Sparta</a> and an alliance of Thebes, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/athens">Athens</a>, Corinth and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/argo">Argos</a>, supported at first by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/persia">Persia</a>. Sparta won on land at Nemea and Coronea but lost its fleet at Cnidus (394 BCE); the war ended with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peace-of-antalcidas">King's Peace</a> of 387 BCE, dictated by the Persian king, which returned the Greek cities of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/asia-minor">Asia Minor</a> to Persia.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/corinthian-war.jpg" alt="Corinthian War" width="320" height="420" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Tilemahos Efthimiadis from Athens, Greece · CC BY 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Grave_relief_of_Dexileos,_son_of_Lysanias,_of_Thorikos_(Ca._390_BC)_(4454389225).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
